<description>
Slide every colored object rightward until it is blocked by the edge or by an object that started farther right.

Input structure
A black-background grid contains several monochromatic foreground objects, each a 4-connected component.

Rule
Clear the foreground, then process objects from right to left by their original bounding boxes.
Each object keeps its shape and color while repeatedly moving one cell to the right until its next step would leave the grid or overlap an already placed object.

Key insight
The objects behave like horizontal gravity: rightmost objects settle first and become blockers, so later objects cannot pass through them even if there is empty space beyond.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "monochromatic non-background 4-connected objects s",
  "path": "each s moves horizontally right one cell at a time, stopping before the grid edge or before any already settled object pixel",
  "trajectory": "paint only the final position of each moved object, preserving its shape and color",
  "transform": "clear all original foreground pixels before placing the settled objects on the background",
  "multi_step": "settle objects in descending original right-edge order; use original bbox position to break ties"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 6-10 rows x 6-13 cols, black background (0)
  objects:
    count: 5-10 monochromatic 4-connected components
    area: 1-5 cells each
    bbox: at most 2x3 (height x width)
    colors: 4-6 distinct non-black colors; duplicates allowed (same color can label separate components)
    density: 10-35% foreground cells
  placement:
    objects do not overlap; at most 2 objects share any single row [observed]
    objects generally occupy left/center portion of grid with free space to their right [observed]
  blocking:
    at least 2 object pairs share rows so that rightward sliding produces object-blocked stops (not just wall stops)
    every example has >=2 objects stopped by another object, and >=2 stopped by the right wall
  transform: slide every object rightward (preserving shape) until blocked by right wall or already-settled object; process right-to-left by original right-edge position

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid dims (6-10 x 6-13) and 5-10 object shapes (small blobs, area 1-5, bbox <=2x3).
    2. Build the OUTPUT by packing objects against the right wall with gravity-like stacking. Place objects right-to-left, each touching the wall or an already-placed neighbor. Ensure >=2 objects are blocked by another object (share rows with a rightward neighbor).
    3. For each object, compute how far left it can slide (its max possible leftward shift = free columns to its left). Choose a random original column offset in [0, max_shift] to get the INPUT position.
    4. Verify no two objects overlap in the derived input and foreground density is 10-35%.
```
</generation_spec>
